{
  "nick": "sfedits",
  "accounts": [
    {
      "template": "{{{page}}} Wikipedia article edited by {{{name}}} {{&url}}",
      "watchlist": {
        "English Wikipedia": {
          "San Francisco Board of Supervisors": true,
          "Daniel Lurie": true,
          "London Breed": true
        }
      },
      "_watchlist_source_comment": [
        "Two source types. Use titles_url to watch a published list of titles,",
        "or project+importance to watch a PageAssessments importance filter.",
        "titles_url wins if both are set. The SFBA deployment uses titles_url",
        "because its task-force importance ratings are measurably uncalibrated",
        "- see docs/importance-ranking-methodology.md. Other regions may find",
        "their ratings perfectly good and should just use project+importance."
      ],
      "watchlist_source": {
        "titles_url": "https://san-francisco-edit-stream.toolforge.org/watchlist-500.json",
        "wikipedia": "English Wikipedia",
        "refresh_hours": 24
      },
      "bluesky": {
        "identifier": "your-username.bsky.social",
        "password": "your-app-password"
      },
      "mastodon": {
        "instance": "https://your-instance.social",
        "access_token": "your-access-token"
      },
      "discord": {
        "webhook_url": "https://discord.com/api/webhooks/your-webhook-id/your-webhook-token"
      },
      "wikidata_claims": {
        "properties": ["P19", "P20", "P131", "P159", "P276", "P937"],
        "refresh_hours": 24,
        "rate_cap": { "max": 5, "window_minutes": 10 }
      },
      "pii_alerts": {
        "bluesky_recipient": "yourpersonalhandle.bsky.social",
        "mastodon_recipient": "yourpersonalhandle"
      },
      "pii_blocking": {
        "enabled": true,
        "blocked_entity_types": [
          "EMAIL_ADDRESS",
          "PHONE_NUMBER",
          "CREDIT_CARD",
          "US_SSN",
          "US_PASSPORT",
          "US_DRIVER_LICENSE",
          "CRYPTO",
          "IBAN_CODE",
          "IP_ADDRESS",
          "URL",
          "PERSON",
          "LOCATION",
          "DATE_TIME",
          "NRP",
          "ORGANIZATION",
          "US_BANK_NUMBER",
          "AU_ABN",
          "AU_ACN",
          "AU_TFN",
          "AU_MEDICARE",
          "IN_PAN",
          "IN_AADHAAR",
          "IN_VEHICLE_REGISTRATION",
          "SG_NRIC_FIN",
          "UK_NHS"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "_topic_store_comment": [
    "The place-bot platform's database. Omit this whole stanza to run the",
    "single-account bot alone: the watchlist above is all it needs. With it,",
    "the bot also serves per-topic subscriptions and /create can open.",
    "On Toolforge, omit user and password - lib/topic-store.js falls back to",
    "TOOL_TOOLSDB_USER and TOOL_TOOLSDB_PASSWORD, which the build service",
    "injects. Setting them here means credentials in a file, which is the",
    "thing SFEDITS_CONFIG exists to avoid. The database must already exist",
    "and be named {your-toolsdb-user}__{name} - see docs/deploy-toolforge.md."
  ],
  "topic_store": {
    "host": "tools.db.svc.wikimedia.cloud",
    "port": 3306,
    "database": "s00000__sfedits",
    "connection_limit": 5,
    "max_posts_per_hour": 20
  },
  "_web_comment": [
    "The webservice: coverage page, place search, and the /create form.",
    "/create stays closed unless BOTH topic_store and a non-empty",
    "invite_codes list are present - the coverage page runs either way.",
    "Treat invite codes as secrets: anyone holding one can create a topic."
  ],
  "web": {
    "invite_codes": ["pick-something-unguessable"],
    "max_articles": 5000
  }
}


